WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.668
China is lashing out at the

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.902
United States after President Joe

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.771
Biden referred to Chinese President

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.706
Xi Jinping as a dictator.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.641
Beijing calling the remark absurd

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.710
and an open provocation.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.745
Let's bring in CNN White House

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.013
correspondent Jeremy Diamond.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.214
Jeremy, is the White House

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.982
standing by the president's

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.751
unscripted remarks about XI?

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.753
And what are the potential impact

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.620
that these comments

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.988
could have on this extremely

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.356
tense relationship?

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.090
Well, this is obviously

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.393
a very delicate moment, Alex, in US-China

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.094
relations, in the US-China relationship.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.562
But the White House is not walking back

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.231
the president's comments at all.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:31.531
In fact,

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.432
a senior administration

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.700
official told me that it should come

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.402
as no surprise that the president

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.002
is speaking

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.437
candidly about China

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.204
and the differences

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.806
between the two countries.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.741
But look, there's no question that inside

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.443
other parts of the US government,

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.644
there was some surprise,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.945
some consternation

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.280
about the fact that the president

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.049
would make these comments publicly.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.550
But remember, these came at a fundraiser

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.851
where there were reporters in the room,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.719
no cameras,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.788
but there were reporters in the room.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:55.555
And the president

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.223
not only referring to Xi

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.158
as a dictator,

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.860
but also essentially undermining

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.363
how she presents his strength

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.297
to the world,

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.032
presenting him as weak, essentially

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.034
noting that she, according to U.S.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.803
intelligence, did not know that

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.303
that spy

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.171
balloon was over

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.639
the United States, drifting over

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.506
the United States

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.208
before the US shot it down.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:15.675
The president

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.677
even saying that she was embarrassed.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.645
And so, again,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.879
a very delicate moment

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:20.680
in the relationship

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.681
between these two countries.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.617
Secretary of State Tony Blinken just left

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.119
Beijing where he had a meeting

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.687
with the Chinese president,

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.289
which was aimed at trying to get

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.491
that relationship back on track.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.625
Now, there are questions

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.927
about whether these comments

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.228
by the president will upend

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.162
that progress.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.030
That senior official

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.730
I reference to you

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.132
earlier, Alex tells me that

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:39.566
they don't

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.934
believe it will, that they believe

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.502
that progress will continue

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.370
and is sustainable going forward.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:44.904
And Jeremy,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.306
there's a meeting at the White House

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.240
tonight with someone else

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.408
who is often accused

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.076
of undemocratic tendencies,

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.711
the prime minister of India,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.047
Narendra Modi, he's visiting Washington.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.915
You have some new reporting on that.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:56.749
Yeah, that's right, Alex.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.118
I'm told that these two leaders

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.052
will indeed hold

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.286
a joint news conference

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.554
tomorrow at the White House,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.356
but that was no small feat.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:03.723
In fact,

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.358
it was the result of intense

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.994
and lengthy negotiations between the U.S.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:08.895
and Indian officials.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.096
I'm told that Indian officials

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.998
initially balked at the idea

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.733
of having a joint news conference

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:14.634
for the two leaders.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.602
The Indian prime minister.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.336
Keep in mind,

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.071
he has never held a news conference

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.339
where he's taking questions

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.306
from reporters.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.841
So ultimately, the U.S.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.976
was initially pushing for a

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.611
to and to two American

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.012
reporters, two Indian reporters

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.780
getting to ask the two leaders questions

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.382
Instead, it will be a one and one.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:29.816
But U.S.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:30.717
officials here

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.352
certainly seeing that as a victory

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:32.819
to get

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.887
the Indian prime minister

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.754
to take questions,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.789
a sign of democratic values.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.223
And, of course,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:37.790
press freedoms

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.025
which we know have eroded

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:39.659
under Modi's

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.327
tenure as Indian prime minister.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.695
This can be a very delicate visit

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.663
for Biden to navigate.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.864
Jeremy Diamond at the White House,

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.099
thanks very much.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.334
Now we have an exclusive CNN report

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.436
on one of the major sources of tension

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.005
between the United States and China,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.606
the future of Taiwan.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.207
CNN chief

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.208
national security correspondent

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.109
Jim Sciutto

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.876
got an inside

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.977
look at how Taiwan's

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.646
military is now preparing

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.048
for a potential invasion by China.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.483
Below, what else?

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.784
Any possibility?

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.953
Commanders of a Taiwanese mechanized

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.388
infantry combat team

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.023
lay out their battle plan.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.258
So coming up, today's mission,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.560
defending the Penghu

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.727
Islands, situated

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.996
right in the middle of the Taiwan Strait

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.531
from a Chinese paratrooper

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.600
assault in rapid succession.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.403
Infantry units storm a captured airfield.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.539
A column of tanks quickly follows

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.608
This maneuver is just a

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.410
training exercise,

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.045
but with a very serious goal

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:32.645
of readying

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:33.446
these forces

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.216
to defend Taiwan from a Chinese invasion.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.585
So in the event of a paratrooper

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.553
assault on the Morgan Airbase,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.487
our troops will be able

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.121
to respond

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.224
instantly and defend the territory.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.660
Exercises like this one are almost daily

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.029
events on Taiwan's Penghu Islands,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.498
less than 100 miles from mainland China.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.334
They are a first line of defense

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.636
for Taiwan against a Chinese invasion

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.705
home to Taiwanese army, air

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.306
force and naval bases.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.774
And not all operations

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.711
for these forces are simulations.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:07.580
The fact is, I visited Penghu for play.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.881
Air Force fighter jets

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.283
entered Taiwan's

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:13.353
Air Defense Identification Zone.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.622
Taiwanese Air Force fighters from a gang

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.657
air base scrambled to respond

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:19.826
before they fly.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.894
They are armed with live ammunition

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:22.895
for combat.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.130
Lieutenant Colonel Bisha

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.966
Kwan has signed Big Commands,

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.135
the Coyote Squadron within your ship.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.170
Sometimes it's reconnaissance.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.239
Sometimes it is training.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.774
Although we're performing combat

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.175
readiness missions here,

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.111
The training has never stopped.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.779
Are you proud of the job you're here?

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.080
Of course.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.715
Taiwanese Navy ships

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.050
based here have had close

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.285
calls of their own.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.820
And they sail with an array of anti-ship

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.155
and anti-air missiles

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.189
to do their part

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.292
in defending against an invasion.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.460
The Taiwanese military here in Peng,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.928
who is engaged

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.164
not just in drills and training,

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:01.367
but in genuine operations, responding

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.703
to Chinese military operations

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.538
in the Taiwan Strait

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.440
And commanders in the Navy,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.575
the Air Force and the Army tell me

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:10.576
their mission

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.612
is to prepare to defend their country.

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:14.280
Taiwan

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.114
buys billions

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.150
of dollars in weapons from the U.S.,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.451
but its defense plan

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.686
depends in large part

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.754
on developing and manufacturing.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.523
Many of its own weapons,

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.758
its indigenous fighter jets

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.293
and many of its Navy frigates

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.997
and EPCs and tanks are all Taiwan built.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.433
That's our territory water.

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:36.836
We won't allow our countries shoot sales

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.739
red launches without permission.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:41.641
On Penghu,

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.141
Taiwanese

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.243
military units are widely dispersed

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.912
for force protection

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.747
to make them more difficult targets

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.248
for any invading force.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.183
There's a saying here.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.884
One commander told me,

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.553
If you want to take Taiwan,

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:56.189
you have to take Peng who first.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.657
And these forces are training

00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:00.159
to make sure that never happens.

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.161
Jim Sciutto, CNN,

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.230
the Penghu Islands, Taiwan

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.699
Thanks to Jim Sciutto for that report.

